    "turn_text": "Yeah, yeah, absolutely. You have a lot of experience with democratic campaigns in Michigan. I feel like if anyone knows how to win a race in Michigan, you've chaired Vice President Al Gore's campaign in Michigan in 2000. And in 2004, you helped secure the general election vote for John Kerry. You, of course, also won your own race and watched your late husband, the longest serving member of Congress, win decades of races. What I'm getting at is you're very familiar with an electorate that people are very curious about. We famously hear often that Trump won Michigan by 11,000 votes. Two months out from the election, how are you feeling and what are you trying? I think you sort of touched on this, but how are you answering constituents questions about who they should maybe vote for, what they should consider as they decide what to do in the next two months?",
