    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/2/92956.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 61,
    "turn_text": "Well, for starters, four years ago, I did tell people that I thought that Donald Trump could become president and people didn't like my saying it. I think that this election is still up in the air and it's why you see so much bitterness and hate out there right now. I think people should ask themselves, are you happy with the direction of the country? Do you think that you're better off than you were four years ago? What's your vision of what you want to be America? Or do I mean our kind of beat? But then I would also ask the question about who's going to be worried about working men and women really? Who's going to fight so that, you know, all of our frontline workers, do you look at where we are now? And in March, all those people that are the glue of our civilized society, Most of them, we didn't think were important enough to pay $15",
